/* book Worked example: Q: A fibre optic link launches 1 mW and receives 0.2 mW after 2 km. Find the loss in dB and in dB/km.
   1. Input power Pin = 1 mW; received power Pout = 0.2 mW; length = 2 km.
   2. Power ratio Pin / Pout = 1 / 0.2 = 5.
   3. Loss in dB = 10 log₁₀(5). log₁₀(5) = 0.69897, so loss = 10 × 0.69897 = 6.9897 dB ≈ 6.99 dB.
   4. Loss per km = 6.9897 dB / 2 km = 3.49485 dB/km ≈ 3.49 dB/km.
   Answer: The loss is 6.99 dB, which is 3.49 dB/km over 2 km. */
