/* book Worked example 2: Q: A fibre for a sensor has core index n1 = 1.50 and cladding index n2 = 1.45. Find (a) the critical angle at the core-cladding boundary, (b) the numerical aperture and (c) the acceptance angle in air.
   1. (a) sin θc = n2/n1 = 1.45/1.50 = 0.9667, so θc = 75.2°, measured from the normal. A ray must meet the boundary at more than 75.2° from the normal, that is at less than 14.8° to the boundary itself, to stay in the core.
   2. (b) NA = √(n1² − n2²) = √(2.25 − 2.1025) = √0.1475 = 0.384.
   3. (c) θa = sin⁻¹(0.384) = 22.6°. Light arriving within a cone of half-angle 22.6° about the axis is guided; steeper rays leak into the cladding.
   Answer: θc = 75.2°, NA = 0.384 and the acceptance half-angle is 22.6°. */
